silm:instances_papers_15_chapters_08_sections_01_concrete_anchor_2#pathlawsetmonicityclaim silm:hasLongDescription "The PathLawSetMonicityClaim is a path-law set asserting designates_A is monic. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'L', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
